WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.480
<b>One-Day Outside Pass — 500 grand
One-Day Suite Pass (A/C, Spa, Videos) — 150 grand
Full Course Dinner — 100 grand
</b>(Western, Japanese, Chinese)
<b>Lunch Combo — 30 grand
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h20 grand</b>

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.200
<i>What is it?</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.690
<i>Agenda 15
\h\h\h\h\h\h<b></b></i>Playing Hard

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.740
I'd like a one-day pass.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>Understood. I'll arrange it.</i>

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.850
<i>Despite being trapped underground, 
he earns large sums of money</i>

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.170
<i>in order to obtain the only ray of hope 
that exists here: the one-day pass.</i>

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.320
<i>The head of Team E, Foreman Ootsuki!</i>

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.380
<i>Several days later, Ootsuki is set free.</i>

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.260
I have to ask, are you sure about this?

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.640
You want to use your one-day pass 
out here with me, Numakawa?

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.770
Sure! As long as you don't mind, Foreman.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.280
The last time I went out on 
my own, it was a real mess.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.880
Well, I don't mind.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.910
The countdown's started!

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.480
Where should we go?! We'd better hurry!

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.080
Now, now, settle down, Numakawa.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.460
Here, read this.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.330
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.460
The first thing you need in order 
to fully enjoy your one-day pass...

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.840
is not to panic.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.930
You need to learn how to relax again.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.360
But...

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.360
That's the monthly edition 
of that magazine, right?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.320
Huh? Yeah.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.110
<i>Ultimately, they spend a relaxed 
hour doing nothing but reading.</i>

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.640
Did you read this new series?

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.050
I did. It was pretty good!

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.750
<i>And they enjoy sharing their 
impressions of the magazines.</i>

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.610
So, what Chiba comics do you like best?

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:50.750
<i>And in time...</i>

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.710
Probably <i>Notari Matsutaro</i> and <i>Ore wa Teppei</i>.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.410
That's just like you!

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.380
<i>...which blooms into a manga discussion!</i>

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.520
All right! Let's grab something to eat.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.040
<i>And finally, they saunter 
over to Nishi-Ogikubo.</i>

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.390
<b>Shirata-ya Pub</b>

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.390
Welcome!

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.090
What are you getting?

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.920
Well, let's see...

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.900
Since it's a special occasion, maybe the 
most expensive thing, this sashimi—

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.900
Seafood

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.900
Seafood Bowl...800 yen

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.900
Assorted Sashimi...2,000 yen

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.900
Pathetic.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.430
<i>Psst...</i>

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.980
Getting what costs the most 
because it's a special occasion...

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.910
Rookies do that all the time.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.790
It's an all-too-common mistake 
when using the one-day pass.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:36.510
Seafood
Seafood Bowl...800 yen
Assorted Sashimi...2,000 yen

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.350
You've lost sight of the real goal here.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.160
The excitement of getting outside

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.080
has made you forget what 
you <i>really</i> want to eat.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:42.050
Fried Delights
Fried Shrimp...420 yen
Chicken Nanban...680 yen
Fried Chicken Cartilage...300 yen
Fried Calamari...260 yen
French Fries...250 yen
Fried Chicken...350 yen

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.050
These last few days in the underground,

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.220
we've been eating nothing 
but bone-dry grilled fish.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.270
Fried food!

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.200
Fried meat, specifically!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.310
Meat?!

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.100
Numakawa, where are you from?

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.710
Uh, M-Miyazaki, over in Kyushu.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.320
I see!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.700
The thing you want to eat, then...

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.700
is chicken nanban!

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.080
That's the best answer!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.050
Thanks for coming!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.800
That chicken nanban was absolutely fantastic!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.600
You were spot-on, Foreman! I can't 
imagine having anything else now!

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.920
See?

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.200
All right, let's head to our second stop.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:26.810
Yeah!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.470
If I recall, there's a nice little 
restaurant over there...

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.820
Huh? Is something wrong, Foreman?

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.930
<i>At that moment, a strange 
premonition enveloped Ootsuki.</i>

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.700
<i>It was the upset feeling that comes from 
having not noticed something important.</i>

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:47.950
<i>Wait a sec...</i>

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.460
<i>His thoughts swirl. His memories flash.</i>

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.360
<i>When we left the pub...</i>

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.340
Foreman?!

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.720
<i>Instinct sends him running!</i>

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.610
<i>Ootsuki rushes forward! Ever forward!</i>

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:20.110
Foreman, wait up! What's gotten into—

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.320
Th-This is...

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:30.830
Numakawa! Does that look like fun or what?!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.810
I love these one-day passes!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.830
<i>It's a blessing! They've stumbled 
upon a summer festival!</i>

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.090
<i>I was right. That woman and her 
daughter were wearing yukatas!</i>

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.110
You're amazing, Foreman!

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.130
Let's do this, Numakawa!

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.010
Yeah!

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.850
<i>It's a change of plans, and before 
long, they're playing hard.</i>

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.600
<i>Yakitori! Yakisoba! And draught beer!</i>

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.190
<i>Both of them more than fill their stomachs!</i>

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.190
I guess we're about done.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.430
All right, for our last stop...

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.610
How do you feel about something starchy?

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.890
Step right up!

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.670
Welcome!

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.870
Which should we get?

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.460
I don't think we can finish both...

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.620
I'll let you make the call, Foreman!

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.880
<i>It was then that divine 
inspiration struck Ootsuki.</i>

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.070
Let me get three servings each of 
takoyaki and okonomiyaki, please.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:30.890
Wha?!

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.970
Good work today, everyone!

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.830
Cheers!

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.400
Hey, excuse me...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.310
Is this the organizers' tent?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.850
Yes, can I help you?

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.410
I just thought you all might 
like to have something to eat!

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.660
Huh?! Really?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.590
Of course, go right on ahead!

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.980
Hey, guys! He brought us food!

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.170
Thank you!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.990
This is great!

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:01.670
<i>This is insane!</i>

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.010
<i>Not only does he do something as 
reckless as buying three of each,</i>

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.680
<i>but then he hands it all over 
to complete strangers?!</i>

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.590
<i>I just can't understand it!</i>

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.060
Here!

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.900
Why don't the two of you join us?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.780
Oh, are you sure?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.060
Well, if you insist!

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.400
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.770
<i>A fine play executed with aplomb by Ootsuki!</i>

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.830
<i>The two of them have now gotten 
their starchy treats... plus alpha!</i>

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.830
<i>With the bonus of free beer 
and company to drink with!</i>

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.580
<i>And they drink all the way until morning!</i>

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.090
<i>A demonstration of the Ootsuki magic!</i>

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.970
<i>Numakawa is dazzled!</i>

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.970
Foreman! Please let me join 
you on your trips from now on!

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.950
Numakawa...

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:59.300
An adventure is only exciting when 
you find your own way, y'know?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:10.110
<b>1 Day Outside Pass</b>

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:10.110
<b><i>Foreman</i></b>

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.620
<i>Ootsuki is released once again, 
after obtaining a one-day pass.</i>

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.120
Here I am in Hibiya...

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.380
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.380
Er...

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.380
Kinda... close, aren't you?

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.910
Closer than usual today...

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.390
The protocols for men in black carrying 
out surveillance on one-day excursions

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.650
don't specify distance to the target.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.490
If a man in black keeps his 
distance during observation,

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.890
it's a sign that he trusts the target.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.730
Do you know what that means, Ootsuki?

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:07.400
My point is, I personally...

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.270
don't trust you one iota!

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.500
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.410
You make a friendly first impression, and 
your reputation underground is good...

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.660
And yet,

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.200
in reality,

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.720
you've been operating these irregular 
games of chinchiro that threaten the order

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.410
in the underground to earn your money!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:29.670
You can trick the others, 
but you won't fool me.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:35.330
Now that I, Miyamoto, am acting as your 
observer, you had better watch yourself!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:40.490
If you act out of line in the slightest, 
I'll drag your ass back underground myself!

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:43.180
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.540
What's so funny?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.830
Oh, nothing... Are you finished?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.960
You need to start the timer.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:53.830
I know that!

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.200
Upsy-daisy...

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.700
<i>The countdown on his 
one-day excursion begins.</i>

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:08.960
<b>Cool Cool Kagoshima Hall</b>

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.770
<i>Ootsuki heads to his first stop:</i>

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.960
<i>an antenna shop selling goods from 
Kagoshima, Cool Cool Kagoshima Hall.</i>

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.960
An antenna shop?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.840
It's a lot of fun to visit places like this.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:16.990
<b>Buzz... buzz...</b>

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.340
<b>Cool Cool
Kagoshima</b>

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.340
Here you go!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.850
Oh, here we go! 
Fried fishcake with lotus root!

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.910
Tasty!

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.710
The texture of the lotus root and 
fried fishcake is fantastic!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.360
Oh, Miyamoto-san...

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.090
What?

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:38.440
I bought one with cheese, too. 
Would you care to try?

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.690
Don't be stupid! I'm on duty!

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.620
Oh, really? Okay.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.090
Tasty!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.750
<b>Heavenly Oita Plaza</b>

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.750
<b>Oita, the Hot Springs Prefecture</b>

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.750
<b>Antenna Shop</b>

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.750
<i>Today's second stop: Heavenly Oita Plaza.</i>

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.070
They let you soak your feet... in the store?!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.090
That really is heavenly!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:03.680
<b>Soak...</b>

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.380
You wanna come over here and join me?

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.850
I told you, I'm on duty right—

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.390
Pathetic.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.660
What?!

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:14.170
You're terrible at relaxing during work.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.610
You won't last long if you're always so tense.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.710
By the way, Miyamoto-san, where are you from?

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.680
Hokkaido, why?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.760
Well, if you're from Hokkaido,

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.520
there's an antenna shop selling stuff 
from there. Just go outside,

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.760
then take the next corner on your right.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:33.440
It's a fairly big one, with lots of 
fresh seafood like crab and salmon roe.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.200
They even sell croquettes 
and soft serve ice cream.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.690
Not that I'm going this time.

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:40.010
Why not?!

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.800
Oh? Did you want to go?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.800
Uh, no...

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:49.170
I already have another antenna shop in mind.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.560
<i>They arrive at Ibaraki Marché, 
representing Ibaraki prefecture.</i>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.070
You're wondering why I 
picked Ibaraki, aren't you?

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.450
The answer is the staff here.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.220
The staff?

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.450
Antenna shops aren't always 
going to be staffed by people

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.030
from the prefecture 
that they're selling from.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.210
If I'm going to shop here,

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:15.080
I'd rather sample the things that 
actual locals would recommend.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:19.590
Bingo!

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:24.220
They're here to support the store! 
The local chamber of commerce!

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.220
<b>Ibaraki</b>

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.770
Since Ibaraki's easy to get to and from,

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.080
I figured it'd be best.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.470
Hey there, mister!

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.160
How about it? You want to 
try drinking a sweet potato?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.730
You can get a cup for 100 yen today!

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.210
<b>Psst...</b>

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.490
Here we go already! A treat 
I've never even heard of!

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.930
We take a sweet potato and 
let it mature for a year!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.360
They end up tasting three 
times sweeter than a melon!

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.240
Three times?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.250
And after we take the time to boil it down,

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.000
we get this tasty sweet potato beverage!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.750
I'll take one, then.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.490
Here you go!

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.590
Amazing!

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.390
It's so rich, but it goes down easy!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.680
See? See?

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.640
What'd I tell you?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.640
It's our potato revolution!

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.630
Go on, buddy, you should have one, too!

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.400
N-No, I'm actually on duty right now...

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.030
<b>Growl...</b>

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:25.990
Caught you!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.180
I'll pay for it.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:30.660
No! Stop it, Ootsuki!

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:37.000
I have to note that despite your 
protests, you're not fighting much.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.670
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.770
No! I...

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.920
Why don't you just be honest with yourself

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:45.690
and enjoy a casual revolution?

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.430
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.530
I am—

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.430
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:59.120
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:06.900
<i>With a single mouthful, 
the Miyamoto Dam collapses!</i>

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.690
<i>Afterward, he snacks on everything</i>

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:15.510
<i>the chamber of commerce recommends!</i>

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.120
<i>And before he notices it,</i>

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.460
<i>he heads to the antenna shop for 
Ishikawa Prefecture: Sakenomiya!</i>

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:25.710
<i>A veritable feast on the local 
specialties of various regions!</i>

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.590
<i>They play hard!</i>

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:33.770
Miyamoto-san, it's almost time.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.400
Who the hell cares?! Another hour won't hurt!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.130
I'm afraid we can't...

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:42.920
I'm telling you, it's fine! 
I personally give you permission!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.050
<i>In the end, they're carried off by the
men in black sent to retrieve them</i>

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.050
Ootsuki, you know your stuff!

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.860
<i>and spend their ride back out cold!</i>

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:53.380
<i>Even when in the clutches 
of the underground prison,</i>

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.280
<i>he seeks to maximize the enjoyment 
of his one-day excursions.</i>

00:14:56.280 --> 00:15:00.880
<i>From the bottom, he seeks 
the top: Foreman Ootsuki!</i>

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:04.370
<i>Where will his next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.320
<i>The next day...</i>

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:14.440
Ootsuki, when's your next trip out?

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:16.180
Can't say for sure.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.970
I'm still the star here.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:28.190
<i>The Cutlet Bog: a battlefield that 
Tonegawa once strode across.</i>

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:28.190
<b>The Cutlet Bog</b>

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.190
<b>Voluminous
Pork Cutlets!</b>

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:33.430
<i>When I first came here, I blew it bigtime.</i>

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.830
<i>That large serving... 
That overwhelming volume...</i>

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.250
<i>But at this point,</i>

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:43.020
<i>I look back at it with a fondness, 
as something from my early days here.</i>

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.580
Welcome!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.560
Do you know what you'd like?

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.970
One pork cutlet bowl.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.260
The ladies' size.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.100
Sure. One ladies' size!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:16:00.860
<i>Yes. The bowls here are arranged on the 
menu according to their actual size.</i>

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:05.410
<i>Anyone who orders the large without 
realizing that is in for hell.</i>

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:08.620
<i>That's why, embarrassing as it might be,</i>

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.900
<i>I'll order the ladies' size 
and be done with it.</i>

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.710
Excuse me, can I get a pork 
cutlet bowl? The large, please.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:17.030
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:17.030
<b>Pork...</b>

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.780
<i>This man is</i>

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.040
<i>a worker in the Teiai underground 
labor camp, the leader of Team E,</i>

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:24.040
<i>Foreman Ootsuki!</i>

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:29.050
<i>This man is the number two 
of the Teiai Group, Tonegawa!</i>

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:33.800
<i>What a coincidence! We find them seated 
next to each other here at the Cutlet Bog!</i>

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.930
A-Are you sure about that? 
The large serving here is...

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:41.210
Oh, it'll be fine. I'm hungrier than usual.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.750
O-Okay.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.690
We've got an order for a large!

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:52.800
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.810
<i>This man has no idea 
about the large size here.</i>

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:53.290
<i>He's just like I once was.</i>

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.700
I'm sorry, sir...

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:58.450
Oh, I know. The large order 
takes priority, right?

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:01.030
<i>That's the rule here at the Cutlet Bog!</i>

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:04.960
<i>When the order for a large comes in, 
it takes priority over the others.</i>

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:08.710
<i>That's common sense to a 
regular such as myself.</i>

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:17.110
<i>I see they still serve up an overwhelming 
and diabolical amount of pork.</i>

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.520
<i>Look at him panic.</i>

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.010
<i>It's useless, I'm afraid.</i>

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:25.230
<i>You made the order, and now you 
have to accept responsibility.</i>

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:27.980
<i>There's nothing unfair about how 
the Cutlet Bog does business.</i>

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.980
<i>It's all there on the menu.
"I didn't realize" won't cut it.</i>

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:39.510
<i>That said, some of the sauces and 
seasonings that aren't on the menu...</i>

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.420
<i>Since I've been through this 
before, I could make use of them</i>

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:45.500
<i>in order to use secret techniques 
to get all that down.</i>

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.500
<i>But I'm not sharing that information!</i>

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.130
Excuse me...

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:55.760
We usually ask people taking on the large 
size if they'd like to be photographed.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.890
Would that be alright?

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.260
A picture?

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.760
<b>The Cutlet Bog is crazy tough...
Captain K-Fuji</b>

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.760
<b>Tokyo Rugby Club, defeated 
Fails to get revenge...!</b>

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.890
<i>There it is! It's like I'm looking 
at a past version of myself.</i>

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:10.650
<i>Now then, I'll kick back 
and enjoy the taste...</i>

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.510
<i>The flavor of safety.</i>

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:15.690
<i>Wha...</i>

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.200
<i>What is with him?</i>

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>He's staring at me!</i>

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:21.450
<i>Wait!</i>

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.330
<b>Is that all?
It was a light snack!</b>

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:23.330
<b>He finished...!
Mr. T-negawa...!</b>

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:33.170
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:39.240
Wow, you managed to get all this 
down! You certainly are spry!

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:41.090
I wouldn't say that...

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:45.280
Oh, I know. If you can handle all that...

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:47.930
Would you like to have some of mine?

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:52.190
By all means, help yourself!

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.690
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.200
There's plenty to go around—

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.950
You're a grown man! 
Don't come running to me for help!

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:03.320
You ordered the large on your own, 
and now you've got what you ordered!

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:06.090
Don't take the Cutlet Bog lightly!

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:09.000
Now, stop your prattling,

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:14.090
and eat your large bowl like a man!

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.460
Sorry about the wait.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.970
Here's your ladies' size bowl.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.970
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.730
You know, I must say...

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.860
You are quite the manly lady.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.980
No... This is just...

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:40.990
Oh, feel free to start eating. 
"Ladies first," as they say.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.580
<i>With that single utterance, a flame is lit!</i>

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>Tonegawa's pride is on fire!</i>

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.500
You're wrong. This is...

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:58.630
What's wrong, exactly?

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:00.720
Hey!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:01.380
Yes?

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:04.890
Bring me what I ordered.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.310
The large!

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.270
<b>Psst...</b>

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.430
S-Sure!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.000
We've got an order for a large!

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:19.330
Magnificent! You're a real man's man, sir.

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:24.300
<i>Out of nowhere, the curtain rises!</i>

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.910
<i>The battle of the large bowls!</i>

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:34.580
<i>Ultimately, both Tonegawa and Ootsuki...</i>

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:40.840
<i>dive into the sea of pork!</i>

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:44.100
Thanks for coming!

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.090
<i>Tonegawa versus Ootsuki!</i>

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:58.360
<i>The winner:</i>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.360
<b>T-negawa falls...!</b>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.360
<b>I can...
keep eating...!</b>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.360
<b>This large
shouldn't count...!</b>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.360
<b>O-tsuki,, KO'd...!</b>

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.360
<i>the pork bowls!</i>

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:05.950
<i>This...</i>

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:10.750
<i>is the story of the battles he waged, 
caught between his own pride</i>

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:13.200
<i>and a massive amount of pork.</i>

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:17.940
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:57.640
Next time, "Natural Enemy."

00:22:56.580 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Natural Enemy</b>
